exports[`cliPages > writes cli/index and one page per command of the recorded help 1`] = `
{
  "cli/check": "---
title: "vibejs check"
description: "Type-check, lint, format-check and test the project with coverage, concurrently."
---

# vibejs check

Type-check, lint, format-check and test the project with coverage, concurrently.

\`\`\`sh
vibejs check [--only types,lint,format,test] [--fix] [--max N]
\`\`\`

## Options

| Option | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`--only\` | string | Run only these steps: types, lint, format, test. |
| \`--fix\` | boolean | Apply lint fixes and format the files first. |
| \`--max\` | string | Show at most N diagnostics (default 20). |

## Examples

\`\`\`sh
vibejs check
vibejs check --only types,lint
vibejs check --fix --max 50
\`\`\`
",
  "cli/docs": "---
title: "vibejs docs"
description: "Look up a VIBE code, open a docs page by path, or search the bundled docs, offline."
---

# vibejs docs

Look up a VIBE code, open a docs page by path, or search the bundled docs, offline.

\`\`\`sh
vibejs docs <query...>
\`\`\`

## Arguments

| Name | Required | Values |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`query\` | yes |  |

## Examples

\`\`\`sh
vibejs docs VIBE8003
vibejs docs errors/VIBE8004
vibejs docs "unknown option"
\`\`\`
",
  "cli/explain": "---
title: "vibejs explain"
description: "Explain a VIBE error code from the bundled catalog, offline."
---

# vibejs explain

Explain a VIBE error code from the bundled catalog, offline.

\`\`\`sh
vibejs explain <code>
\`\`\`

## Arguments

| Name | Required | Values |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`code\` | yes |  |

## Examples

\`\`\`sh
vibejs explain VIBE8003
\`\`\`
",
  "cli/index": "---
title: "CLI reference"
description: "Every vibejs command, its options and examples."
---

# CLI reference

Run \`vibejs <command> --help --json\` for the same reference as JSON.

| Command | Summary |
| --- | --- |
| [\`vibejs explain\`](./explain.md) | Explain a VIBE error code from the bundled catalog, offline. |
| [\`vibejs docs\`](./docs.md) | Look up a VIBE code, open a docs page by path, or search the bundled docs, offline. |
| [\`vibejs check\`](./check.md) | Type-check, lint, format-check and test the project with coverage, concurrently. |

## Global options

| Option | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`--json\` | boolean | Print one JSON object (on by default in agent mode). |
| \`--help\`, \`-h\` | boolean | Describe the commands and their options. |
| \`--version\` | boolean | Print the vibejs version. |
",
}
`;

exports[`llms > writes llms.txt: title, disambiguation, every non-error page once, no error codes 1`] = `
"# vibe.js

> vibe.js: npm scope \`@usevibejs\`, CLI \`vibejs\` (never \`vibe\`). Not monday.com Vibe (\`@vibe/*\`), not the \`@vibe.js/*\` packages (a different project), not the npm packages \`vibejs\` or \`vibe.js\`.

Offline docs for the installed version: \`node_modules/@usevibejs/cli/dist/docs/\`. Explain an error code with \`vibejs explain VIBE####\`.

- [Fixture home](https://vibejs.org/v0/): The fixture landing page.

## Guides

- [guides/no-title](https://vibejs.org/v0/guides/no-title)
- [Getting: started](https://vibejs.org/v0/guides/start): Start here.

## Server

- [Handlers](https://vibejs.org/v0/server/handlers)

## Zeta

- [Notes](https://vibejs.org/v0/zeta/notes)

## Optional

- [Error codes](https://vibejs.org/v0/errors/): every VIBE error code with its message and fixes
- [Full docs](https://vibejs.org/v0/llms-full.txt): every page, error pages included, in one file
"
`;

exports[`llms > writes llms-full.txt: every page once, error pages last 1`] = `
"# Fixture home

Read [the guide](https://vibejs.org/v0/guides/start) or [an error](https://vibejs.org/v0/errors/VIBE0001).

Source: https://vibejs.org/v0/

---

# guides/no-title

Just prose.

Source: https://vibejs.org/v0/guides/no-title

---

# Getting: started

Intro without a title heading; see [the handlers](https://vibejs.org/v0/server/handlers#ctx).

> **Tip:**
> Use the CLI.

> **Careful now:**
> Do not cast.
>
> \`\`\`ts
> const one: number = 1;
> \`\`\`
>

\`\`\`ts {2}
export const base: string = DOCS_BASE;
\`\`\`

\`\`\`sh
# not a title
\`\`\`

Source: https://vibejs.org/v0/guides/start

---

# Handlers

See [the home page](https://vibejs.org/v0/), [an external page](https://example.com) and [the context](#ctx).

## Ctx

Each handler receives one typed context.

Source: https://vibejs.org/v0/server/handlers

---

# Notes

Source: https://vibejs.org/v0/zeta/notes

---

# Error codes

| Code                      | Title         | Package | Status |
| ------------------------- | ------------- | ------- | ------ |
| [VIBE0001](https://vibejs.org/v0/errors/VIBE0001) | Fixture error | errors  |        |

Source: https://vibejs.org/v0/errors/

---

# VIBE0001: Fixture error

> The fixture failed.

### Example

\`\`\`ts
const broken: number = 'not checked';
\`\`\`

Source: https://vibejs.org/v0/errors/VIBE0001
"
`;

